   "spoken": "One honest miss: Black had Nb4, forcing the bishop's surrender. The clean answer is Be4 then back to d3, inducing d5 to lock the centre — an ugly-looking but sound Jobava-London structure, because after the freeing c5, dxc5 and d4 reforms a healthy centre.",
